From f01c06f44fbf72c4ee29135f0a00b219c1e7524b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:25:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] env: build the web write candidate from the baseline
 block alone

The /env request staged its candidate from the RAM environment and then
aligned it against flash. That path persisted a key the request never
named (t92d): a second export overwrote the buffer that held the tweak
keys, the restore called env_set() with garbage names and corrupted the
RAM environment, and the next no-change write persisted the difference.

Build the candidate from the flash baseline block alone instead: copy
every baseline entry with its original bytes and order, and only replace
or append the one key named in the request. The RAM environment no
longer takes part, so a request naming only bootdelay cannot persist any
other key, whatever the RAM environment contains. The block is
serialized directly (never parsed before the write), and the requested
key is applied to the RAM environment only after the write verified.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
---
 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631env.c       |  69 +++++----
 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631env_build.h | 192 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 237 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631env_build.h

